/Title (Most of us try to avoid, push away, or numb uncomfortable feelings. It works in the short term, but over time the avoided things get bigger, and life gets smaller: skipped classes or meetings, cancelled plans, avoided conversations, more screen-time escape, less of what we love. ACT calls this experiential avoidance. The more we struggle, the more stuck we get, like quicksand.)
